## Plan

## Summary

Move the `[DESIGNING]`→`[DESIGNED]` title rename in `design-publish.sh` to immediately after architecture-diagram upsert, dropping the `PUBLISH_OK==true` gate and not introducing a scrub gate for admission. Rename runs when `SESSION_ID` is non-empty. A later `design-log-publish.sh` failure, skipped flush, or unmerged log PR must not block `/implement`.

Keep a `design-log-publish.sh --scrub-only` preflight, but make it a log-publish preflight after admission rename, not an admission gate. If scrub-only fails closed, skip the full flush, report log-publish failure/recovery, and leave `[DESIGNED]` admission intact when rename succeeded. If scrub-only reports redactions with `SCRUB_OK=true`, emit an immediate operator-visible SECURITY diagnostic before full flush and dedupe the final WARN. Stale `final-summary.md` cleanup must run before scrub-only/full publish.

When `SESSION_ID` is empty, admission is explicitly blocked (`ADMISSION_READY=false`, `ADMISSION_BLOCK_REASON=session-id-missing`) so Step 5d/footer/render never imply `/implement` may proceed.

Accepted review revisions add: Step 5c parser support for new result keys; decouple Step 5c item 6 rename/admission prose from `PUBLISH_OK` (Step 6 cleanup stays `PUBLISH_OK`-gated); `set +e` scrub-only capture; full flush skipped on `SCRUB_OK=false`; `SCRUB_OK=false` tests asserting no flush; stale-summary cleanup before scrub checks; `DESIGN_PUBLISH_RENAME_NOOP` live export; `SECURITY.md` update; scrub-only tests covering `git push` side effects; Step 5d/footer split on admission state; scrub-failed recovery via direct `design-log-publish.sh` rerun (not `/design` Step 5c retry after `[DESIGNED]`); rotation only for `SECRET_SCRUB_VIOLATIONS`.

SIMPLE-tier reorder in `design-publish.sh` and `design-log-publish.sh`, plus contracts, test harnesses, `SECURITY.md`, and stale admission/operator prose. `/implement` Preflight behavior remains title/body-keyed.

